; X2AccessCompanion localization — the reference file. Every key the companion speaks in its own
; words is here, under the class that declares it (X2AccessVocab holds all of them; see the class
; header and docs/localization.md). A language file that lacks a key speaks nothing for it, so
; translate against this list.
;
; Templates use the game's own tags: <XGParam:IntValue0/>, <XGParam:IntValue1/>,
; <XGParam:IntValue2/> for numbers and <XGParam:StrValue0/> for a name or a phrase. Move the tag to
; wherever your language wants the number; never remove one the English line carries.
;
; A counted noun is three keys, _One, _Few and _Many, chosen by PluralRule. English uses One for
; exactly 1 and Many otherwise, so Few is left empty here. A language with a few-form sets
; PluralRule="slavic" and fills all three (2-4 and 22-24 take Few; 11-14 take Many).

[X2AccessVocab]
PluralRule=""

NoUnitSelected="No unit selected"
Tiles_One="<XGParam:IntValue0/> tile"
Tiles_Few=""
Tiles_Many="<XGParam:IntValue0/> tiles"
